From ff2a1bf0faf49fdcbe9868dd90f3fe0e4010c869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:49:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give the tab sheet predictive back, a width cap, TalkBack and
 glass.

Back closes the sheet. It is modal, so like Material's modal bottom
sheets it goes away rather than stepping down to half. While the back
gesture is held the sheet shrinks toward its toolbar, and it springs
back if the gesture is cancelled. The page never sees that back.

From 600dp wide the sheet is at most 640dp and centered. A window under
440dp tall, such as a phone on its side, has no room for a half stop, so
the sheet opens full there, and one at half goes full when turned.

The handle row is a 48dp target that TalkBack reaches as the drag
handle, with its state and expand, collapse and dismiss actions, and
settling at a stop is announced. The scrim and the overlay behind the
sheet are skipped by TalkBack.

Frosted glass now applies to the sheet. Its blur window ends at the
toolbars, so they stay sharp, untinted and tappable. Focusing a text
field outside the sheet, such as the address bar, closes it, so the
keyboard and suggestions are not left under it.

A rebind the tab list ran when its animations ended could land inside a
layout pass and crash; it now runs after the pass.

The side drawer is unchanged.

Tested on the Android emulator (Pixel 10 Pro profile).
